          "description": "File and Directory Permissions Modification: Linux and Mac"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "course-of-action",
      "spec_version": "2.1",
      "id": "course-of-action--19c82238-54c1-5295-a514-bd92cd56b708",
      "created": "2026-06-10T18:01:52.000Z",
      "modified": "2026-06-10T18:01:52.000Z",
      "created_by_ref": "identity--930a2431-32e6-5652-ae5b-e36316353d39",
      "name": "CTFTCTE-PWN-009 - Pre-plant a symlink over a privileged fixed-name output path",
      "description": "1. Inventory every fixed path the privileged binary writes to (strings, Ghidra, or a quick strace -f run): default output folders, config paths, temp names. 2. From a writable directory, pre-plant a symlink with that exact name pointing at the target you cannot write to directly (classic target: /root/.ssh to land an authorizedkeys). 3. Feed the tool an input that makes it write a payload file through the symlink (for an archive extractor: a tar whose root entry is authorizedkeys with your public key). 4. Verify with a low-privilege test write first; keep a second payload entry in the archive in case ordering matters.",
      "x_ctft_category": "PWN",
      "x_ctft_domain": "PWN",
      "x_ctft_role": "resolution",
      "external_references": [
        {
