          "description": "Exploitation for Privilege Escalation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "course-of-action",
      "spec_version": "2.1",
      "id": "course-of-action--d27be844-cc88-5bf8-979e-4ad54000362f",
      "created": "2026-06-10T18:01:52.000Z",
      "modified": "2026-06-10T18:01:52.000Z",
      "created_by_ref": "identity--930a2431-32e6-5652-ae5b-e36316353d39",
      "name": "CTFTCTE-PWN-011 - Control argument registers, then redirect",
      "description": "Read the expected values from the decompiled argument checks, then deliver them at the moment of the jump: assemble a register-setting chain from the available gadgets (pop reg; ret), fall back to call-oriented setup (ret2csu-style) when an individual gadget is missing, keep stack alignment for callees using SSE, and on i386 pass the arguments on the stack instead. Map parameters to registers by ABI order (rdi, rsi, rdx, rcx, r8, r9), never by which constant \"looks like\" which register.",
      "x_ctft_category": "PWN",
      "x_ctft_domain": "PWN",
      "x_ctft_role": "resolution",
      "external_references": [
        {
