      "created_by_ref": "identity--930a2431-32e6-5652-ae5b-e36316353d39",
      "name": "CTFTTE-PWN-012 - Author-gifted pointer leak",
      "description": "The binary deliberately prints a raw pointer before reading input — a stack address (leaking ASLR/stack layout, enabling stack shellcode or ret2win without guessing) or a .data/.bss address (leaking the PIE image base so win's runtime address can be computed). Hardening stays on (PIE/ASLR) but the author hands the one leak needed to defeat it, and the solver must do the offset arithmetic.",
      "kill_chain_phases": [
        {
          "kill_chain_name": "ctft",
          "phase_name": "pwn"
        }
